# Backend Testing Architecture (Five S Framework)

Drafting a comprehensive testing architecture for our NestJS monorepo microservice backend. This setup supports **Unit Tests**, **Integration Tests**, and **End-to-End (E2E) Tests** completely isolated from production/development data, using high-fidelity mocks, Factory patterns, and database synchronization scripts.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Isolation Strategy**: We will create and isolate separate testing databases (`db_user_test`, `db_scheduler_test`, `db_teamwork_test`) so that local developers and CI/CD pipelines can run tests safely without wiping or contaminating dev data.
> We will configure a centralized startup helper to automatically run `prisma db push` on all schemas against test databases before E2E testing starts.

> [!TIP]
> **Mocking External Services**: High-fidelity mocks will be implemented for external platforms including AI agents (Gemini/OpenAI), Redis Cache, Socket.io clients, Giphy Stickers, Cloudinary, and Nodemailer.

---

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> 1. Do you have any preference for the test database credentials, or should we reuse the default `studyplan:secret` on `localhost:5432`? (Proposed default: Yes, we will reuse them but point to isolated database names like `db_user_test`).
> 2. Is there any active CI environment where you want these test runners to execute automatically? If not, we will configure standard `package.json` scripts (`pnpm test`, `pnpm test:integration`, `pnpm test:e2e`) so that you can run them easily on your machine and plug them into any future CI/CD engine.

